From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:09:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] UserAgentManager: Firefox for Android's by default

The desktop string with "Mobile;" added still gets the desktop layout
from many sites; Firefox for Android's gets the mobile one. As the
default it follows the running Firefox version, where a user.js pin
(Firefox/159 on Firefox 160 on the Galaxy Z Flip3) goes stale. The
per-site rules are unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 src/modules/UserAgentManager.sys.mjs | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/modules/UserAgentManager.sys.mjs b/src/modules/UserAgentManager.sys.mjs
index 81f0bd9..064a7e1 100644
--- a/src/modules/UserAgentManager.sys.mjs
+++ b/src/modules/UserAgentManager.sys.mjs
@@ -19,8 +19,10 @@ export class UserAgentManager {
           "Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 10; K) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/154.0.8037.59 Mobile Safari/537.36";
     const UA_CHROME_CHROMEOS =
           "Mozilla/5.0 (X11; CrOS aarch64 16765.51.0) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/152.0.7977.132 Safari/537.36";
-    // Set default user agent
-    PrefManager.defaultPref('general.useragent.override', UA_FIREFOX_MOBILE);
+    // Set default user agent: Firefox for Android's, so sites serve their mobile
+    // layout; "X11; Linux x86_64; Mobile" gets the desktop one from many of them.
+    // It follows the running Firefox version, unlike a pinned user pref.
+    PrefManager.defaultPref('general.useragent.override', UA_FIREFOX_ANDROID);
 
     const userAgentRules = {
         // Google
-- 
